WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.963
Campaign material accumulates like weather.

2
00:00:09.963 --> 00:00:19.926
Notes, districts, NPCs, rulings, handouts, recaps, lore, and all the strange little campaign details that only make sense after the fifth session have a way of drifting into separate corners.

3
00:00:19.926 --> 00:00:29.889
RUNBOOK PRESS turns that drifting mass into an artifact with intention. A primer. A district guide. A mission packet. A season book.

4
00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:39.852
A handoff worthy of the campaign that created it. Structure matters here. What the players can know. What the GM must protect.

5
00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:49.815
What belongs in the appendix.

6
00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:59.778
What needs to be findable in five seconds when the room is waiting and the night is already moving.

7
00:00:59.778 --> 00:01:09.741
Layout is not decoration. It is retrieval under pressure. When a new player joins, the book should welcome them into the season.

8
00:01:09.741 --> 00:01:19.704
When the campaign ends, it should leave behind something the table wants to keep. RUNBOOK PRESS is not about export.

9
00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:29.667
It is about memory made readable.
